{"slug":"setup-task-system","title":"The Task System","blocks":[{"id":"b1","type":"ingress","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Barkpark as your AI's task board: the agent claims work over HTTP, you steer the same queue in the browser Studio, and every change broadcasts to both sides in real time."}]},{"id":"b2","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Tasks are plain "},{"type":"text","value":"type:task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" documents — no second store, no sync. A root task is a "},{"type":"text","value":"goal","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"; children nest under it; dependencies form a graph; claims are atomic and fenced so many workers can't trample each other."}]},{"id":"b3","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"What you get"},{"id":"b4","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Surface"}],[{"type":"text","value":"What"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Studio Tasks pane","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"A "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks ✅","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" desk group at "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" with lifecycle tabs; editor = four-group dossier (brief · work · close · system); "},{"type":"text","value":"dependencies","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" read-only."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"`bp` verbs","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"bp task ls / ready / prime / events / get / next / claim / release / stamp / pulse / landed / close / move","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" — manifest-driven."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Terminal TUI","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"bp tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (= "},{"type":"text","value":"bp task tui","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); "},{"type":"text","value":"c","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"text","value":"x","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" claim/close as "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_WORKER_ID","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"text","value":"tui-<hostname>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). Keys: tui cheatsheet."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"HTTP API","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Bearer endpoints under "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (read tier): the verbs plus fetch, edges, labels, papers."}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Events","marks":["strong"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Each op emits a "},{"type":"text","value":"mutation_events","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" row — "},{"type":"text","value":"task.{claimed,released,criterion,pulse,closed,mutated,relabeled,referenced,reparented,lease_expired,compacted,compaction_restored}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"Push","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" SSE "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/data/listen/:dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"text","value":"pull","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" keyset feed "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/events?since=<id>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (§7)."}]]]},{"id":"b5","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle: "},{"type":"text","value":"open · in_progress · blocked · done · cancelled","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b6","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Set up from zero"},{"id":"b7","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Install and run the wizard per QUICKSTART."}]},{"id":"b8","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The wizard's "},{"type":"text","value":"clean profile pre-checks `bulldocs` + `tasks`","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" (server unions "},{"type":"text","value":"media","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); accept and schema, routes and crons go live on first boot. A dev server on "},{"type":"text","value":":4000","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" blocks the local DB reset — stop it or pick "},{"type":"text","value":"connect","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b9","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing installs","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" — enable via env and restart:"}]},{"id":"b10","type":"code","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS=bulldocs,tasks  # CSV whitelist · unset = all plugins · empty = kill switch"},{"id":"b12","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" schema auto-registers each boot (idempotent on "},{"type":"text","value":"(name, dataset)","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"); two Oban crons ride along: lease sweeper, compaction (6 h)."}]},{"id":"b13","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Point an AI agent at it"},{"id":"b14","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Token.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Any bearer token works for the task endpoints (read tier — claim/close are workflow ops, not document mutations). Creating tasks goes through the mutate endpoint, which needs an admin token. Dev default: "},{"type":"text","value":"barkpark-dev-token","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b15","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Discover.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" One call teaches the whole surface:"}]},{"id":"b16","type":"code","value":"bp capabilities -o json  # = GET $API/v1/capabilities, bearer"},{"id":"b17","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Create tasks.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Standard mutation envelope. Required: "},{"type":"text","value":"kind: \"task\"","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" + a valid "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". Optional: "},{"type":"text","value":"priority","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (0–4, 0 = highest), "},{"type":"text","value":"assignee","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"labels","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"papers","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", dossier fields ("},{"type":"text","value":"brief","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"description","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"acceptance_criteria","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"purpose","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"estimate","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"due_at","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"outcome","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", …) — the "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" schema is authoritative. "},{"type":"text","value":"brief","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" = the PortableDoc envelope ("},{"type":"text","value":"{version: 1, blocks: […]}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"text","value":"description","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" its text fallback; author briefs as blocks, not a text wall. "},{"type":"text","value":"bp task create \"<title>\" --yes","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" files a draft; "},{"type":"text","value":"--publish","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" also needs "},{"type":"text","value":"--description","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (20+ chars) and 1–12 tags already registered as "},{"type":"text","value":"type:tag","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" docs ("},{"type":"text","value":"bp doc ls tag --all","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":") — an invented tag is refused before anything is created."}]},{"id":"b18","type":"code","value":"curl -X POST $API/v1/data/mutate/production -H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"mutations\":[{\"create\":{\"_type\":\"task\",\"_id\":\"t1\",\"title\":\"Ship the docs\",\"content\":{\"kind\":\"task\",\"lifecycle_status\":\"open\",\"priority\":1}}}]}'"},{"id":"b19","type":"callout","tone":"info","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Draft prefix note:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"create","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" always lands as a draft (stored id "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"). The task endpoints resolve the bare id "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" automatically — you can use either "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". If both a published "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and a draft "},{"type":"text","value":"drafts.t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" exist, "},{"type":"text","value":"t1","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" matches the published row (exact match wins). Task lifecycle is independent of draft/publish; publishing a task is optional."}]},{"id":"b20","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"4. The claim → work → close loop.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Pick a stable "},{"type":"text","value":"worker_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" per agent."}]},{"id":"b21","type":"code","value":"bp task next agent-1          # queue claim, priority order; prints doc_id + epoch; no_ready (HTTP 200, not an error) when empty\nbp task claim t1 agent-1      # targeted claim: <doc_id> <worker_id>\nbp task release t1 agent-1 1  # voluntary walk-away, fenced: <doc_id> <worker> <epoch>\n\n# Mid-claim: stamp a criterion. --criterion N is ZERO-based (0 = the first). Take the wording\n# from a FILE (`-` = stdin): a double-quoted `code span` is COMMAND SUBSTITUTION FROM THE ROW,\n# which matches any index and leaves the guard INERT.\nbp task get t1 -o json | jq -r '.doc.content.acceptance_criteria[0].criterion' > crit.txt\nbp task stamp t1 agent-1 1 --criterion 0 --criterion-text-file crit.txt --met --evidence \"gate green\"\nbp task stamp t1 agent-1 1 --criterion 1 --miss --note \"flaky\"\nbp task stamp t1 agent-1 1 --criterion 0 --criterion-text-file crit.txt --withdraw --note \"wrong branch\"\n# A pulse renews the 45 min lease AND BUMPS claim.epoch: stamp/close on the PULSE's epoch, not the claim's.\nbp task pulse t1 agent-1 --now \"warm-up pinned, rerunning\" --criterion 2\n\nbp task close t1 agent-1 1    # epoch-fenced: <doc_id> <worker> <epoch> [status] [reason]\n# Close with evidence: flips ride the same rev-CAS — but a flip made HERE is not proof of itself.\nbp task close t1 agent-1 1 --set 'criteria:=[{\"index\":0,\"met\":true,\"evidence\":\"PR #123\",\"criterion\":\"gate passes\"}]'\n# Landing from CI: no worker, no epoch; --criterion N seals ONE merge-shaped row\nbp task landed t1 --commit a1b2c3d --pr 123 --note \"merged to main\" --criterion 6"},{"id":"b22","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Full contract — what each verb fences on, every refusal ("},{"type":"text","value":"409 fenced_off","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"not_holder","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"criteria_unmet","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", …), and "},{"type":"text","value":"--withdraw","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", the only verb that LOWERS a met flag (a bare "},{"type":"text","value":"met:true → met:false","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" patch is refused everywhere), including its sealed-row rules: claim-lifecycle; close receipt: close-packet."}]},{"id":"b24","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Dependencies, labels, papers.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Same bearer + JSON headers as the mutate call above; the routes are in the cheatsheet. "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks/edges","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"{\"from_id\":\"t2\",\"to_id\":\"t1\"}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" = t2 waits on t1 — from = dependent, to = blocker, "},{"type":"text","value":"kind","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" defaults "},{"type":"text","value":"blocks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/:id/edges","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" takes "},{"type":"text","value":"?kind=all","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b26","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Filtered reads.","marks":["strong"]}]},{"id":"b27","type":"code","value":"bp task ready --limit 5 --offset 0  # deterministic queue page\nbp task ready --all                 # aggregate pages\nbp task ls --limit 20               # all tasks, goals included"},{"id":"b28","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Filters: "},{"type":"text","value":"kind","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"phase_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"parent","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"label","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"type","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"limit","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (index default 1000; "},{"type":"text","value":"ready","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and the bp verbs default 50)."}]},{"id":"b29","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"7. Watch the stream.","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" Both routes are in "},{"type":"text","value":"What you get","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"text","value":"Push:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" SSE, "},{"type":"text","value":"task.*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", no polling. "},{"type":"text","value":"Pull:","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"bp task events --since <id>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" replays id-ASC, one page (≤500): "},{"type":"text","value":"{ok, events:[{id,event,doc_id,rev,at}], cursor, has_more}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"text","value":"id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is the stable cursor (monotonic PK). Resume with the last "},{"type":"text","value":"cursor","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; omit = from start; "},{"type":"text","value":"has_more:true","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → poll again. One "},{"type":"text","value":"dataset","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (default "},{"type":"text","value":"production","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"), "},{"type":"text","value":"type=task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":"b30","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Working with your AI in Studio"},{"id":"b31","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"text","value":"/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" → the "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks ✅","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" group. The division of labour:"}]},{"id":"b32","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"You (Studio form)"}],[{"type":"text","value":"The agent (API)"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"Flip "},{"type":"text","value":"lifecycle_status","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (5-state dropdown), set "},{"type":"text","value":"priority","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"text","value":"assignee","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":", edit titles/descriptions"}],[{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"close","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" with fencing, add edges, relabel, link papers"}]],[[{"type":"text","value":"Triage: open new tasks, cancel dead ones"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Drain the ready queue in priority order"}]]]},{"id":"b33","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"The terminal TUI edits the flat fields (title, description, lifecycle, priority, …) and carries the claim/close quick actions ("},{"type":"text","value":"c","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"text","value":"x","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on a task list or in a task's editor — same fenced endpoints the agent uses); composite dossier fields like "},{"type":"text","value":"acceptance_criteria","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" are Studio- and API-editable only (the documented v1 TUI constraint). "},{"type":"text","value":"dependencies","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"text","value":"claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" show as read-only pretty-printed JSON in the editor — round-tripping structured values through a text input would corrupt them, so the form simply never submits those fields and the API stays the single writer. Everything updates live via PubSub: when the agent claims a task, your pane reflects it without a refresh."}]},{"id":"b34","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Goals and phases"},{"id":"b35","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Everything is a task. The pattern:"}]},{"id":"b36","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[[{"type":"text","value":"Goal","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a root task (no "},{"type":"text","value":"parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":")."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Phase / subtask","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a task whose "},{"type":"text","value":"content.parent_id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is the parent's doc id."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Rail","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" = a task's chronological children: "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks?parent=<id>","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" (oldest first); "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/:id","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" inlines one level of "},{"type":"text","value":"children","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" summaries + "},{"type":"text","value":"child_count","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}],[{"type":"text","value":"Scope a worker to one phase: "},{"type":"text","value":"POST /v1/tasks/claim","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"text","value":"{\"worker_id\":…,\"phase_id\":…}","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"text","value":"GET /v1/tasks/ready?phase_id=…","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]]},{"id":"b37","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Goal → phases → leaf tasks, with "},{"type":"text","value":"blocks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" edges sequencing the phases, gives you a multi-phase project board in a standard Barkpark install."}]},{"id":"b38","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Workspaces, projects, datasets — experiment without mess"},{"id":"b39","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Any write-tier token spins up an isolated sandbox:"}]},{"id":"b40","type":"code","value":"bp workspace create Spike  # → workspace + owner + Default project + production dataset\nbp -w spike workspace project-create agents-v2  # member-gated; -w names the workspace\nbp workspace ls  # what your token can reach"},{"id":"b41","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Scoped Studio: "},{"type":"text","value":"/w/:workspace_slug/p/:project_slug/studio","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":"; scoped data routes mirror the prefix; flat "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" uses the server's default scope."}]},{"id":"b42","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Troubleshooting"},{"id":"b43","type":"table","head":[[{"type":"text","value":"Symptom"}],[{"type":"text","value":"Cause → fix"}]],"rows":[[[{"type":"text","value":"No "},{"type":"text","value":"Tasks","marks":["strong"]},{"type":"text","value":" pane in Studio, or "},{"type":"text","value":"404","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"text","value":"/v1/tasks/*","marks":["code"]}],[{"type":"text","value":"Plugin off — pane and routes mount only when "},{"type":"text","value":"tasks","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" is on: "},{"type":"text","value":"BARKPARK_PLUGINS","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" set without it, or the "},{"type":"text","value":"task","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" schema isn't registered. Fix env + restart; the schema auto-registers on boot."}]]]},{"id":"b44","type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","value":"Cheatsheet: "},{"type":"text","value":"../cheatsheets/tasks.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" · CLI canon: "},{"type":"text","value":"../cli/HANDBOOK.md","marks":["code"]},{"type":"text","value":" · HTTP contract: "},{"type":"text","value":"../api-v1.md","marks":["code"]}]}],"related":["decisions-deferred","cheatsheets-http-api","cheatsheets-tasks","cli-handbook","api-v1"]}
